    "result_text": "Tests are green and the JSON renders identically through the shared mapper.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agreed with both findings:\n\n1. **Dropped the hand-rolled JSON serializer.** Removed `toJson()` and the private `quote(...)` escaper from `OwnerCreatedEvent`, making it a pure data record. The audit step now serializes the event through the shared `ObjectMapper` (injected as a Spring bean parameter, the same mechanism the responders use via `ObjectResponse<T>`): `AUDIT.info(objectMapper.writeValueAsString(event))`. The emitted line is byte-for-byte the same as before, so acceptance behaviour is unchanged.\n\n2. **Trimmed the redundant rationale.** The \"current primary identifier\" intent now lives in the `OwnerCreatedEvent` record's javadoc as the single source of truth; the inline comment in `service(...)` is reduced to a one-line pointer (`// customerCode is the owner's current primary identifier (see OwnerCreatedEvent).`).\n\nThe `SEQUENCE` counter and the record's compact convenience constructor (which the reviewer liked) are untouched. Full suite: `BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures.\n\nNote on `writeValueAsString`: under Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson`) it throws only the unchecked `JacksonException`, so no checked-exception handling is needed in the function signature.",
